## 4. PROFILE MANAGEMENT

Implement a complete profile management section.

### Profile fields

Support the fields appropriate to the existing user model:

- Full name or display name.
- Email address.
- Profile avatar, if supported.
- Optional phone number, if supported by the existing application and authentication provider.
- Account creation date, displayed as read-only when available.

Do not collect unnecessary personal information.

### Functionality

Users should be able to:

- View their current profile.
- Edit their display name.
- Update supported profile fields.
- Upload or change an avatar if storage infrastructure exists.
- Remove their avatar if supported.
- Save changes and see updated values.
- Cancel edits.
- Reload the page and see persisted changes.

Validate required fields, length limits, and formats.

For email changes, use the authentication provider's verified email-change process. Do not simply update the profile table and treat the new address as verified.

If the authentication provider requires confirmation through the old or new email address, follow that workflow and display the actual verification status.

Never allow users to edit protected fields such as their internal user ID, role, access permissions, or account ownership.

### Avatar upload security

If avatar uploads are supported:

- Validate file type and size.
- Use safe storage paths scoped to the user.
- Prevent unauthorized access to private storage.
- Avoid accepting arbitrary executable files.
- Handle upload failures gracefully.
- Use existing storage infrastructure rather than introducing an unnecessary service.

If avatar infrastructure does not exist and cannot be added safely in this phase, provide a polished initials-based avatar instead of a broken upload button.

