## 6. TIMEZONE MANAGEMENT

Implement a timezone preference if the existing application can support it reliably.

### Requirements

- Detect the browser's timezone as a suggested initial value when appropriate.
- Allow users to choose a supported timezone.
- Save the selected timezone to the authenticated user's preferences.
- Display dates and times consistently with the saved preference.
- Keep database timestamps in the existing canonical storage format, usually UTC where applicable.
- Avoid shifting date-only transaction fields because of timezone conversion.
- Handle daylight-saving transitions correctly when supported by the chosen date/time library.

Clearly distinguish between date-only financial records and timestamps.

A transaction recorded for a particular calendar date should not unexpectedly appear on the previous or following day merely because a display preference changed.

If complete timezone support would require a larger architectural change, implement the safe parts and document any remaining limitations rather than applying inconsistent conversions.

