## 10. SESSION AND DEVICE MANAGEMENT

Inspect the existing authentication provider to determine whether session listing and revocation are supported.

If supported, implement:

- A list of active sessions or devices.
- Available session metadata from the provider.
- A way to revoke a selected session.
- A secure sign-out-from-other-sessions action, if supported.
- Confirmation before revoking sessions.
- Refreshing the session list after a successful operation.

Never invent sessions or device information.

Do not expose access tokens, refresh tokens, cookies, or other session secrets.

If the provider does not expose session-management APIs, do not fabricate this capability. Explain the limitation and preserve the existing logout functionality.

